==English==
{{wikipedia|River Clyde}}

===Etymology===
The name of a river in Scotland, from the {{w|Gaelic}} name [[Cluaidh]], of uncertain origin. Possibly influenced by ''clut'' (“the cleansing one”).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/klaɪd/}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪd}}
* {{homophone|en|clied}}

